      {
        "math_academy_id": "q-102705",
        "knowledge_point_id": "c89778fa-3c8d-5f0a-a0f8-c9b3d9193ffd",
        "knowledge_point": "Solving a 2x2 System of Equations Using an Inverse Matrix",
        "problem": "Which of the following represents the solution to the system of linear equations given below?\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-2x+2y=1 \\\\ 2x-3y=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$",
        "worked_solution": "This system can be written as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}].$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{(-2)\\cdot (-3)-2\\cdot 2}[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$",
        "answer_fields": [
          {
            "key": "selection",
            "type": "radio",
            "choices_complete": true,
            "choices": [
              {
                "type": "math",
                "value": "x=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]",
                "option": "0",
                "source_option": "a"
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "value": "x=\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]",
                "option": "1",
                "source_option": "b"
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "value": "x=\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]",
                "option": "2",
                "source_option": "c"
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "value": "x=2[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]",
                "option": "3",
                "source_option": "d"
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "value": "x=\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]",
                "option": "4",
                "source_option": "e"
              }
            ],
            "correct_value": "x=\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]",
            "value_type": "math",
            "correct_type": "math",
            "evidence": {
              "kind": "worked_solution",
              "value": "x=\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]",
