      {
        "math_academy_id": "q-103836",
        "knowledge_point_id": "6a18aadb-3e8a-54d7-a5d7-e78208e77675",
        "knowledge_point": "Describing Properties of the Cotangent Function",
        "problem": "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡x?$ Assume $n$ is an integer.\n\nI. The function has vertical asymptotes at $x=\\pi +\\frac{n\\pi }{2}.$\n\nII. The domain of the function is $[-\\pi ,\\pi ].$\n\nIII. The period of the function is $\\pi .$",
        "worked_solution": "Let's plot the graph of $y=cot⁡x.$\n\n![](images/77/7785ad73f6e5212772c3053780ffd055f37cfb39927b6ddc3e40cd3a55b8ba4e.png)\n\nNow, let's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false. The vertical asymptotes of the function are integer multiples of $\\pi $, i.e., $x=n\\pi .$\n\n- Statement II is false. The domain of the function is all real numbers except the values where the asymptotes occur, i.e., $x=n\\pi .$\n\n- Statement III is true. The period of $y=cot⁡x$ is $\\pi .$",
