      {
        "math_academy_id": "q-1051",
        "knowledge_point_id": "3f9ccaa5-d69c-584d-946e-0c57b3050160",
        "knowledge_point": "Finding the Augmented Matrix of a System of Linear Equations",
        "problem": "What is the augmented matrix for the following system of linear equations?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}6x+y+z=4 \\\\ x+z=9\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
        "worked_solution": "First, we organize the system so that the variables are ordered $x,y,z$ on the left-hand side, the constants are on the right-hand side, and every variable has a coefficient:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}6x+y+z=4 \\\\ x+0y+z=9\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe coefficient matrix consists of the coefficients of the variables:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}6 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe augmented matrix  is the coefficient matrix augmented with the column that represents the right-hand sides of the equations:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}6 & 1 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 & 9\\end{aligned}]\n$$",
