        "knowledge_point_id": "900dcaf8-da39-5654-96cd-6aec89e379c9",
        "knowledge_point": "Calculating Joint Probabilities",
        "problem": "The marginal mass functions of the independent discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ are shown below. Given that the corresponding joint probability mass function is $f(x,y),$ find $f(3,1).$\n\n<table align=\"center\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">$x$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$3$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">${f}_{X}(x)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.3$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.5$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p></p></th>\n<th width=\"50\"></th>\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">$y$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\">${f}_{Y}(y)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.25$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.75$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p></p></th></tr></tbody></table>",
        "worked_solution": "Two discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ with joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ are independent if and only if \n\n$$\nf(x,y)={f}_{X}(x)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(y)\n$$\n\n \n\nfor all possible values $x$ and $y,$ where ${f}_{X}(x)$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ are the marginal probability mass functions for $X$ and $Y,$ respectively.\n\nTherefore, since our discrete random variables are independent, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(3,1) & ={f}_{X}(3)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(1) \\\\  & =0.5\\cdot 0.25 \\\\  & =0.125.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
        "answer_fields": [
          {
            "key": "selection",
            "type": "radio",
            "choices_complete": true,
            "choices": [
              {
                "type": "math",
                "value": "0.25",
                "option": "0",
                "source_option": "a"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "value": "Impossible to determine using the given information.",
                "option": "1",
                "source_option": "b"
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "value": "0.5",
                "option": "2",
                "source_option": "c"
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "value": "0.125",
                "option": "3",
                "source_option": "d"
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "value": "0.025",
                "option": "4",
                "source_option": "e"
              }
            ],
            "correct_value": "0.125",
            "value_type": "math",
            "correct_type": "math",
            "evidence": {
              "kind": "worked_solution",
              "value": "0.125",
              "source_file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14085343/state.json",
              "solution_quote": "\\begin{aligned}f(3,1) & ={f}_{X}(3)\\cdot {f}_{Y}(1) \\\\  & =0.5\\cdot 0.25 \\\\  & =0.125.\\end{aligned}",
              "matches_worked_solution": true,
              "choice_present": true
            }
          }
        ],
