      {
        "math_academy_id": "q-111032",
        "knowledge_point_id": "e247e2c9-3e47-5cf4-be8d-f1f22bb30b39",
        "knowledge_point": "Calculating a Joint Probability Containing Inequalities From a Table",
        "problem": "|  | $Y=2$ | $Y=3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ |\n| $X=2$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ |\n\nCompute $P(X=2)$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above.",
        "worked_solution": "Using the values in the table, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=2) & =P((X,Y)\\in \\{(2,2),(2,3)\\}) \\\\  & =P((X,Y)=(2,2))+P((X,Y)=(2,3)) \\\\  & =f(2,2)+f(2,3) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}+\\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
        "answer_fields": [
