      {
        "math_academy_id": "q-122496",
        "knowledge_point_id": "b6b720d4-59b0-5d86-b856-ff69abfe4152",
        "knowledge_point": "Evaluating Combinations Given Using Alternate Notation",
        "problem": "Evaluate $(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{12}{2}).$",
        "worked_solution": "First, note that $(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{12}{2})$ means the same thing as ${}_{12}{C}_{2}.$\n\n In general, the number of combinations of $n$ objects taken $r$ at a time is given by the formula\n\n$$\n{}_{n}{C}_{r}=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!\\,r!}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=12$ and $r=2,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{}_{12}{C}_{2} & =\\frac{12!}{(12-2)!2!} \\\\  & =\\frac{12!}{10!2!} \\\\  & =\\frac{12\\cdot 11\\cdot \\cancel{10!}}{\\cancel{10!}\\cdot 2} \\\\  & =66.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
        "answer_fields": [
          {
            "key": "selection",
            "type": "radio",
