      {
        "math_academy_id": "q-12284",
        "knowledge_point_id": "c89778fa-3c8d-5f0a-a0f8-c9b3d9193ffd",
        "knowledge_point": "Solving a 2x2 System of Equations Using an Inverse Matrix",
        "problem": "Which of the following represents the solution to the system of linear equations given below?\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}5x-2y=3 \\\\ 2x-y=5\\end{aligned}\n$$",
        "worked_solution": "This system can be written as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}].$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{5\\cdot (-1)-(-2)\\cdot 2}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{-1}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$",
        "answer_fields": [
