        "math_academy_id": "q-12490",
        "knowledge_point_id": "fd3b5e36-46db-5d34-92e2-eefb7e0e95c8",
        "knowledge_point": "Finding the First Few Terms of a Binomial Expansion",
        "problem": "${(x+7y)}^{10}=$",
        "worked_solution": "The binomial theorem states that for any positive integer $n,$ we have\n\n \n\n$$\n(a+b)^{n}=(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{0}){a}^{n}{b}^{0}+(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{1}){a}^{n-1}{b}^{1}+(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{2}){a}^{n-2}{b}^{2}+…+(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{n}){a}^{0}{b}^{n}.\n$$\n\nIn the case of ${(x+7y)}^{10},$ we have  $a=x,$ $b=7y,$ $n=10.$ \n\nTherefore, the first three terms of ${(x+7y)}^{10}$ are as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(x+7y)}^{10} & =(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{10}{0}){(x)}^{10}{(7y)}^{0}+(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{10}{1}){(x)}^{10-1}{(7y)}^{1}+(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{10}{2}){(x)}^{10-2}{(7y)}^{2}+… \\\\  & =1{(x)}^{10}+10{(x)}^{9}{(7y)}^{1}+45{(x)}^{8}{(7y)}^{2}+… \\\\  & =1({x}^{10})+10({x}^{9})(7y)+45({x}^{8})(49{y}^{2})+… \\\\  & ={x}^{10}+70{x}^{9}y+2\\,205{x}^{8}{y}^{2}+…\\end{aligned}\n$$",
        "answer_fields": [
