        "math_academy_id": "q-129232",
        "knowledge_point_id": "f5d1d859-0b86-5507-a7bf-3d805a85adf3",
        "knowledge_point": "Identifying Augmented Matrices in Row Echelon Form",
        "problem": "Which of the following augmented matrices are **not** in row echelon form?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -4 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 6 & 7\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 3 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 9 & 6 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 5\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & -4 & 5 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & -7 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 5 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
        "worked_solution": "Remember that an augmented matrix is in row echelon form if its coefficient matrix satisfies the following conditions:\n\nI. All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the *bottom* of the matrix.\n\nII. Each leading entry of a row is in a column *to the right* of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is not in row echelon form since ${a}_{33}\\ne 0$ (condition II is violated).\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -4 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 6 & 7\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is not in row echelon form since the third row contains only zeros and it is not at the bottom of the matrix (condition I is violated).\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 3 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 9 & 6 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is not in row echelon form since ${c}_{33}\\ne 0$ (condition II is violated).\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & -4 & 5 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & -7 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 5 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, $A,$ $B,$ and $C$ are **not** in row echelon form.",
