      {
        "math_academy_id": "q-129604",
        "knowledge_point_id": "52e51c9a-6bce-5ea6-a9fe-febb09f8754d",
        "knowledge_point": "Solving a System of Equations Given an Augmented Matrix Containing Non-Unit Leading Entries",
        "problem": "Solve the system of equations represented by the augmented matrix: \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
        "worked_solution": "The matrix represents a system of three linear equations in three variables, say, $x$, $y$, and $z.$ We obtain the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned} & 4x+y+2z=-3 \\\\  & y+3z=0 \\\\  & -z=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third equation states that \n\n$$\n-z=1\\,⟹\\,z=-1.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny+3(-1)=0\\,⟹\\,y=3.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute $z=-1$ and $y=3$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\n4x+(3)+2(-1)=-3\\,⟹\\,x=\\frac{-3-3+2}{4}=-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-1$, $y=3$, and $z=-1.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as \n$[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].$",
