      {
        "math_academy_id": "q-129615",
        "knowledge_point_id": "52e51c9a-6bce-5ea6-a9fe-febb09f8754d",
        "knowledge_point": "Solving a System of Equations Given an Augmented Matrix Containing Non-Unit Leading Entries",
        "problem": "Solve the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned} & {x}_{1}+5{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=-1 \\\\  & -{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=7 \\\\  & 2{x}_{3}=4\\end{aligned}\n$$",
        "worked_solution": "The third equation states that \n\n$$\n2{x}_{3}=4\\,⟹\\,{x}_{3}=2.\n$$\n\n Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n-{x}_{2}+3(2)=7\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=6-7=-1.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute ${x}_{3}=2$ and ${x}_{2}=-1$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+5(-1)+(2)=-1\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=-1+5-2=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is \n${x}_{1}=2$, ${x}_{2}=-1$, and ${x}_{3}=2.$  In vector form, the solution can be written as $[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$",
