      {
        "math_academy_id": "q-130455",
        "knowledge_point_id": "5a870c4a-daa5-5df2-8968-d8bf9ac0bd75",
        "knowledge_point": "Identifying True Statements Regarding Matrix Multiplication",
        "problem": "Given that $A,B,$ and $C$ are $6\\times 6$ matrices which of the following statements are always true? \n\nI. $A(BC)=(AB)C$\n\nII. $A(B-C)=AB-CA$\n\nIII. $CA=AC$",
        "worked_solution": "Let's consider the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is true. Matrix multiplication is associative and  $A(BC)=(AB)C$ is always true.\n\n- Statement II is false. Matrix multiplication is distributive, so $A(B-C)=AB-AC,$ but $AC\\ne CA$ because matrix multiplication is not commutative in general.\n\n- Statement III  is false. Matrix multiplication is not commutative, so $CA\\ne AC$ in general.\n\nTherefore, only statement  I is true.",
        "answer_fields": [
          {
            "key": "selection",
            "type": "radio",
            "choices_complete": true,
            "choices": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "value": "II and III only",
                "option": "0",
