      {
        "math_academy_id": "q-131499",
        "knowledge_point_id": "65f742e7-89c6-543b-b43a-f41c27f35abf",
        "knowledge_point": "Finding the General Solution of a Singular 3x3 System of Equations with One Pivot",
        "problem": "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -8 & 6 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFind the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix.",
        "worked_solution": "The system corresponding to $M$ is\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2x-8y+6z=-4 \\\\ 0x+0y+0z=0 \\\\ 0x+0y+0z=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince any numbers $x,y,z$ form a solution of the final two equations $0x+0y+0z=0,$ we can remove these equations from the system. So, our system now consists of just a single equation:\n\n$$\n2x-8y+6z=-4\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variable is $x$, and we have two free variables $y$ and $z.$ That means we need to find $x$ in terms of $y,z.$ Doing this, we get\n\n$$\nx=4y-3z-2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=4y-3z-2 \\\\ y=y \\\\ z=z,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $y$, $z$ (free variables) are arbitrary numbers.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4y-3z-2 \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+y[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+z[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
        "answer_fields": [
          {
