      {
        "math_academy_id": "q-13771",
        "knowledge_point_id": "e69a4aee-6e92-598b-99b5-1d830b6dea54",
        "knowledge_point": "Identifying Correct Statements About a Matrix",
        "problem": "Consider the matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}8 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}].$\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $A$ is upper triangular\n\nII. $A$ is lower triangular\n\nIII. ${A}^{T}+A$ is lower triangular",
        "worked_solution": "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true, since all the entries below the main diagonal are zeros:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}8 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true, since all the entries above the main diagonal are zeros:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}8 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true, since the result of $A+{A}^{T}$ has all the entries above the main diagonal equal to zero: \n\n$$\n{A}^{T}+A=[\\begin{aligned}16 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III\".",
        "answer_fields": [
          {
            "key": "selection",
            "type": "radio",
            "choices_complete": true,
            "choices": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "value": "I and III only",
                "option": "0",
                "source_option": "a"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "value": "I only",
                "option": "1",
                "source_option": "b"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "value": "II and III only",
                "option": "2",
                "source_option": "c"
