      {
        "math_academy_id": "q-142575",
        "knowledge_point_id": "96473ec4-67f8-5614-b187-0961062aac29",
        "knowledge_point": "Finding a Cumulative Probability Given a Joint Distribution",
        "problem": "| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $\\frac{3}{7}$ | $\\frac{1}{7}$ |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{2}{7}$ | $\\frac{1}{7}$ |\n\nGiven the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ above for the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y,$ calculate $P(Y<2).$",
        "worked_solution": "If the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have joint distribution with joint probability mass function $f(x,y),$ then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=x) & ={f}_{X}(x)={\\sum }_{y}f(x,y) \\\\ P(Y=y) & ={f}_{Y}(y)={\\sum }_{x}f(x,y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${f}_{X}(x)$ and ${f}_{Y}(y)$ are the marginal mass functions for $X$ and $Y,$ respectively.\n\nIn this case, the marginal distribution for $X$ corresponds to the row totals, and the marginal distribution for $Y$ corresponds to the column totals. Let's add these row and column totals to our table:\n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | ${f}_{X}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $\\frac{3}{7}$ | $\\frac{1}{7}$ | $\\frac{4}{7}$ |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{2}{7}$ | $\\frac{1}{7}$ | $\\frac{3}{7}$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}$ | $\\frac{5}{7}$ | $\\frac{2}{7}$ | $1$ |\n\nThe marginal mass function for $Y$ is given in the following table:\n\n| $y$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $\\frac{5}{7}$ | $\\frac{2}{7}$ |\n\nFinally, using the table of values of the marginal mass function for $Y,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Y<2) & =P(Y\\in \\{1\\}) \\\\  & =P(Y=1) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
        "answer_fields": [
          {
            "key": "selection",
            "type": "radio",
            "choices_complete": true,
            "choices": [
              {
                "type": "math",
                "value": "\\frac{4}{7}",
