        "problem": "Let $I=[0,2]⊂R$ and ${X}_{i}=[0,i]\\times \\{-i\\}.$ Which of the following represents ${⋂}_{i\\in I}{X}_{i}?$",
        "worked_solution": "Recall that the intersection of a family of indexed sets consists of those elements that belong to *all* the sets:\n\n$$\n{⋂}_{i\\in I}{A}_{i}=\\{x\\,:\\,x\\in {A}_{k}\\,\\,\\text{for all}\\,\\,k\\in I\\}\n$$\n\nLet's now write down one of our indexed sets. For example, if $i=1,$ we have \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}=[0,1]\\times \\{-1\\}=\\{(k,-1)\\,:\\,k\\in [0,1]\\}.\n$$\n\nThis represents a horizontal line segment from the point $(0,-1)$ to the point $(1,-1)$ in the coordinate plane, as shown below.\n\n![](images/a3/a39443fd1b3764ff60c0c052085134ad7eeda6759c07c4d936fc03cd121f72dd.png)\n\nIn general,\n\n$$\n{X}_{i}=[0,i]\\times \\{-i\\}=\\{(k,-i)\\,:\\,k\\in [0,i]\\}\n$$\n\nis the horizontal line segment from the point $(0,-i)$ to the point $(i,-i).$ \n\n![](images/7f/7f18af14c55acc4bc2cd63b601dba0bde3cd51c0284b398b401c854537003926.png)\n\nThere are no points that lie in all sets. Therefore, the intersection of the indexed sets is $∅,$ the empty set.",
