      {
        "math_academy_id": "q-177651",
        "knowledge_point_id": "6290e701-b4ea-5a86-ab7e-7371c5bdc11e",
        "knowledge_point": "Visualizing Unions of Uncountable Families of Indexed Sets",
        "problem": "Let $I=[0,1]⊂R$ and ${X}_{i}=[-i,i]\\times \\{2i\\}.$ Which of the following represents ${⋃}_{i\\in I}{X}_{i}?$",
        "worked_solution": "Recall that the union of a family of indexed sets consists of those elements that belong to *at least one* set:\n\n$$\n{⋃}_{i\\in I}{A}_{i}=\\{x\\,:\\,x\\in {A}_{k}\\,\\,\\text{for at least one}\\,\\,k\\in I\\}\n$$\n\nLet's now write down one of our indexed sets. For example, if $i=0.5,$ we have \n\n$$\n{X}_{0.5}=[-0.5,0.5]\\times \\{1\\}=\\{(k,1)\\,:\\,k\\in [-0.5,0.5]\\}.\n$$\n\nThis represents a horizontal line segment from the point $(-0.5,1)$ to the point $(0.5,1)$ in the coordinate plane, as shown below.\n\n![](images/6c/6c6aafd9ea78868e953340eaab3862491d275972d690e2ceb27c213dadbcaea6.png)\n\nIn general,\n\n$$\n{X}_{i}=[-i,i]\\times \\{2i\\}=\\{(k,2i)\\,:\\,k\\in [-i,i]\\}\n$$\n\nis the horizontal line segment from the point $(-i,2i)$ to the point $(i,2i).$ \n\n![](images/02/02c8f93a25d7b510d3e238e6d4a974d6ccc2e83f3ac01fe92ce4535fbb4dce48.png)\n\nAs $i$ runs over $I,$ these line segments sweep the following triangle that represents the union ${⋃}_{i\\in I}{X}_{i}:$\n\n![](images/3b/3b3cefa03d71d99e4b7f3b6852ed36512d2a841a37c558034eac5c4b6870799c.png)",
        "answer_fields": [
          {
