      {
        "math_academy_id": "q-181306",
        "knowledge_point_id": "c3a2b291-c6dd-58c8-a10f-d851511d7bfc",
        "knowledge_point": "Sketching Cartesian Products in the Coordinate Plane",
        "problem": "Which of the following is a representation of the set $S=[-1,1]\\times \\{-1,1\\}$ in the Cartesian plane?",
        "worked_solution": "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\n$$\nA\\times B=\\{(a,b)\\,:\\,a\\in A,\\,b\\in B\\}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the set \n\n$$\nS=[-1,1]\\times \\{-1,1\\}\n$$\n\ncontains every point in ${R}^{2}$ whose $x$-coordinate is any real number in the interval $[-1,1]$ and whose $y$-coordinate is either $-1$ or $1.$\n\n$$\nS=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,x\\in [-1,1],\\,y\\in \\{-1,1\\}\\}.\n$$\n\nTo visualize $S$, consider ${S}_{1}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate is any real number in the interval $[-1,1]$ and whose $y$-coordinate equals $-1$\n\n$$\n{S}_{1}=\\{(x,-1)\\,:\\,x\\in [-1,1]\\}\n$$\n\nThis set is represented by the line segment shown below.\n\n![](images/3e/3ed05ffc58aad1a6c75e7862c1175f497fb14870e6650cc6c4ce01c3df091d8b.png)\n\nNext, consider ${S}_{2}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate is any real number in the interval $[-1,1]$ and whose $y$-coordinate equals $1$\n\n$$\n{S}_{2}=\\{(x,1)\\,:\\,x\\in [-1,1]\\}.\n$$\n\nThis set is represented by the line segment shown below.\n\n![](images/0f/0f57920b2532177b0d64ac3dc95feb6a476bb385112d736d702895862e7de2b2.png)\n\nOur Cartesian product is the *union* of these subsets:\n\n$$\nS={S}_{1}\\cup {S}_{2}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $S$ can be represented by the two line segments shown below.\n\n![](images/07/075454dae9ed36967a70537cdf3a3f59931cdd81671ff4059658d2e0df438898.png)",
