      {
        "math_academy_id": "q-181959",
        "knowledge_point_id": "e2aee319-68d6-54f7-8023-b24d32610bc4",
        "knowledge_point": "Sketching Cartesian Products of Special Sets in the Coordinate Plane",
        "problem": "Which of the following is a representation of the set $S=N\\times Z$ in the Cartesian plane?",
        "worked_solution": "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\n$$\nA\\times B=\\{(a,b)\\,:\\,a\\in A,\\,b\\in B\\}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the set \n\n$$\nS=N\\times Z\n$$\n\ncontains every point in ${R}^{2}$ whose $x$-coordinate is a natural number and whose $y$-coordinate is an integer number.\n\n$$\nS=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,x\\in N,\\,y\\in Z\\}.\n$$\n\nTo visualize $S$, consider ${S}_{1}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate equals $1$ and whose $y$-coordinate is any integer number.\n\n$$\n{S}_{1}=\\{(1,y)\\,:\\,y\\in Z\\}.\n$$\n\nWe can represent ${S}_{1}$ in the plane as follows:\n\n![](images/17/179fdaa3921cb29f2d25ff97bce262fd13fb2ff591c12e97a33953e95967f6fc.png)\n\nNext, consider ${S}_{2}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate equals $2$ and whose $y$-coordinate is any natural number.\n\n$$\n{S}_{2}=\\{(2,y)\\,:\\,y\\in Z\\}.\n$$\n\nWe can represent ${S}_{2}$ in the plane as follows:\n\n![](images/73/7399e42988df8a809013393d8873b6a6e5f60b64c0419eadd7bb3c334eb410d6.png)\n\nWe can create the subsets ${S}_{3},{S}_{4},{S}_{5},…$ similarly. Our Cartesian product $S$ is the *union* of these subsets:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S & ={S}_{1}\\cup {S}_{2}\\cup {S}_{3}\\cup … \\\\  & ={⋃}_{i\\in N}{S}_{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can visualize $N\\times Z$ as the set of points in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/16/16ff13c793d3c3f57eefee638fbc1ff83569ef6d084d9d053f8585f72c8812d7.png)",
        "answer_fields": [
