      {
        "math_academy_id": "q-184505",
        "knowledge_point_id": "6290e701-b4ea-5a86-ab7e-7371c5bdc11e",
        "knowledge_point": "Visualizing Unions of Uncountable Families of Indexed Sets",
        "problem": "Let $I=[0,1]⊂R$ and ${X}_{i}=\\{i\\}\\times [0,{i}^{3}].$ Which of the following represents ${⋃}_{i\\in I}{X}_{i}?$",
        "worked_solution": "Recall that the union of a family of indexed sets consists of those elements that belong to *at least one* set:\n\n$$\n{⋃}_{i\\in I}{A}_{i}=\\{x\\,:\\,x\\in {A}_{k}\\,\\,\\text{for at least one}\\,\\,k\\in I\\}\n$$\n\nLet's now write down one of our indexed sets. For example, if $i=0.5,$ we have \n\n$$\n{X}_{0.5}=\\{0.5\\}\\times [0,0.125]=\\{(0.5,k)\\,:\\,k\\in [0,0.125]\\}.\n$$\n\nThis represents a vertical line segment from the point $(0.5,0)$ to the point $(0.5,0.125)$ in the coordinate plane, as shown below.\n\n![](images/3a/3a1bb7a7c54718e39df80092243a119ec8b5a6e77ec4f9d58ffb074e50191d04.png)\n\nIn general,\n\n$$\n{X}_{i}=\\{i\\}\\times [0,{i}^{3}]=\\{(i,k)\\,:\\,k\\in [0,{i}^{3}]\\}\n$$\n\nis the vertical line segment from the point $(i,0)$ to the point $(i,{i}^{3}).$ \n\n![](images/47/472b6456019a5c89e585f80aa4a0dfd44f3b87c0624c10ea7b52f32e958a8c4e.png)\n\nAs $i$ runs over $I,$ these line segments sweep the following figure that represents the union ${⋃}_{i\\in I}{X}_{i}:$\n\n![](images/20/204c9a31031534ac70a599322c3f77a077440300fde2364476643c88406e34cd.png)",
        "answer_fields": [
          {
