      {
        "math_academy_id": "q-29608",
        "knowledge_point_id": "4241c7bd-4a2b-556f-be9f-8a884addebb9",
        "knowledge_point": "Describing Properties of the Tangent Function",
        "problem": "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x?$ Assume that $n$ represents any integer.\n\nI. The function has asymptotes at $x=n\\pi .$\n\nII. $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x)=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x+2n\\pi ).$\n\nIII. The range of the function is $[-1,1].$",
        "worked_solution": "Let's recall the graph of $y=tan⁡x.$\n\n![](images/31/31b430f003171dcc04a8f17402d6035fbbc305c244d3676bbf5da83fa447bd50.png)\n\nLet's examine each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false. The function $y=tan⁡x$ has asymptotes at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\pi n.$\n\n- Statement II is true. The function has period $\\pi .$ So, $tan⁡(x+2n\\pi )=tan⁡(x+n\\pi +n\\pi )=tan⁡(x+n\\pi )=tan⁡(x).$\n\n- Statement III is false. The range of $y=tan⁡x$ is $(-\\infty ,+\\infty ).$",
        "answer_fields": [
          {
