      {
        "math_academy_id": "q-38547",
        "knowledge_point_id": "81247553-750f-5bf7-a1c4-698ad63b5ae4",
        "knowledge_point": "Identifying True Statements Regarding Left- and Right-Continuity",
        "problem": "![](images/18/188e0169738a08b3d4580b4f5d3a3ab1aedef87a9d1b83f07c1b10686a38c321.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true in relation to the function $y=g(x)$ above?\n\nI. The function is left-continuous at $x=0$\n\nII. The function is right-continuous at $x=0$\n\nIII. The function is continuous at $x=0$",
        "worked_solution": "Let's look at each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is false. The function is not left-continuous at $x=0,$ since the left-sided limit is not equal to the function value:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {0}^{-}}g(x)=0\\ne -2=g(0)\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. The function is right-continuous at $x=0,$ since the right-sided limit is equal to the function value:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}g(x)=-2=g(0)\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. In order for the function to be continuous at $x=0,$ it must be both left-continuous and right-continuous. However, we have already determined that the function is not left-continuous at this point.\n\nIn conclusion, only statement II is true.",
        "answer_fields": [
          {
            "key": "selection",
            "type": "radio",
            "choices_complete": true,
            "choices": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "value": "II and III only",
                "option": "0",
                "source_option": "a"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "value": "I and III only",
                "option": "1",
                "source_option": "b"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "value": "II only",
                "option": "2",
                "source_option": "c"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "value": "I and II only",
                "option": "3",
                "source_option": "d"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "value": "I only",
                "option": "4",
                "source_option": "e"
              }
            ],
            "correct_value": "II only",
            "value_type": "text",
