      {
        "math_academy_id": "q-42449",
        "knowledge_point_id": "4ad1721d-26a4-5459-bc81-297ff0e4d678",
        "knowledge_point": "Solving a 3x3 System of Equations By Calculating the Inverse of the Coefficient Matrix",
        "problem": "Solve the following system of linear equations by finding the inverse of the coefficient matrix:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2x-3+z=0 \\\\ 5y-1+3x=2z+1 \\\\ 3z+2x-1=2y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind  $x+y+z.$",
        "worked_solution": "First, let's rewrite the system in the correct order:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+z=3 \\\\ 3x+5y-2z=2 \\\\ 2x-2y+3z=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we  write the system in the form $Ax=b$, where $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $x$ and $b$ are $3\\times 1$ column vectors. We can do this as follows:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 5 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$ So, we compute ${A}^{-1}$ as follows:\n\n*Step 1:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 5 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2|\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}|-0+|\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2(15-4)+(-6-10) \\\\  & =22-16 \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\n*Step 2:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}11 & 13 & -16 \\\\ 2 & 4 & -4 \\\\ -5 & -7 & 10\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 3:*\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}11 & -13 & -16 \\\\ -2 & 4 & 4 \\\\ -5 & 7 & 10\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n*Step 4:*\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}11 & -2 & -5 \\\\ -13 & 4 & 7 \\\\ -16 & 4 & 10\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n*Step 5:*\n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T}=\\frac{1}{6}[\\begin{aligned}11 & -2 & -5 \\\\ -13 & 4 & 7 \\\\ -16 & 4 & 10\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, the solution to the given system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}[\\begin{aligned}11 & -2 & -5 \\\\ -13 & 4 & 7 \\\\ -16 & 4 & 10\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}[\\begin{aligned}24 \\\\ -24 \\\\ -30\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, $x+y+z=4-4-5=-5.$",
        "answer_fields": [
          {
            "key": "selection",
            "type": "radio",
            "choices_complete": true,
            "choices": [
              {
                "type": "math",
                "value": "3",
                "option": "0",
                "source_option": "a"
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "value": "-5",
                "option": "1",
                "source_option": "b"
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "value": "13",
                "option": "2",
                "source_option": "c"
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "value": "-6",
                "option": "3",
                "source_option": "d"
              },
              {
