              "source_file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14076826/state.json",
              "solution_quote": "If $k\\ne 1$, then the system $[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & k\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$ has the unique zero solution.",
