      {
        "math_academy_id": "q-82034",
        "knowledge_point_id": "3eaed693-68df-5da8-942d-408d6871358a",
        "knowledge_point": "Finding the Real or Imaginary Part of a Scalar Given the Conjugate of a Scaled Vector",
        "problem": "Find $\\text{Re}(k)$ given that\n$v=[\\begin{aligned}-4+8\\text{i} \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$\\overset{―}{kv}=[\\begin{aligned}20 \\\\ -4+8\\text{i}\\end{aligned}].$",
        "worked_solution": "Since $\\overset{―}{kv}=\\overset{―}{k}\\,\\overset{―}{v},$ we get the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{kv} & =\\overset{―}{k}\\,\\overset{―}{v} \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}20 \\\\ -4+8\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] & =\\overset{―}{k}\\,\\overset{―}{[\\begin{aligned}-4+8\\text{i} \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]} \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}20 \\\\ -4+8\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] & =\\overset{―}{k}\\,[\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{-4+8\\text{i}} \\\\ \\overset{―}{4}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}20 \\\\ -4+8\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] & =\\overset{―}{k}\\,[\\begin{aligned}-4-8\\text{i} \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}20 \\\\ -4+8\\text{i}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}(-4-8\\text{i})\\overset{―}{k} \\\\ 4\\overset{―}{k}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}(-4-8\\text{i})\\overset{―}{k}=20 \\\\ 4\\overset{―}{k}=-4+8\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get \n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{k}=-1+2\\text{i}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation, we obtain the true statement\n\n$$\n(-4-8\\text{i})(-1+2\\text{i})=20.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $k=\\overset{―}{-1+2\\text{i}}=-1-2\\text{i}.$\n\nFinally, $\\text{Re}(k)=-1.$",
        "answer_fields": [
