      {
        "math_academy_id": "q-97521",
        "knowledge_point_id": "b4844e17-9365-5a6f-a5f4-b9fa83fd81e1",
        "knowledge_point": "Computing a Probability Over an Interval Using the Complement",
        "problem": "Given that $X∼B(7,0.5),$ compute $P(X\\le 6).$ Round your final answer to $4$ decimal places.",
        "worked_solution": "For a binomial random variable $X∼B(n,p),$ we have the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{x}){p}^{x}(1-p)^{n-x}\n$$\n\nHere, we have $X∼B(7,0.5),$ so $X$ has the probability mass function\n\n$$\nf(x)=(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{7}{x})(0.5)^{x}(0.5)^{7-x}.\n$$\n\nComputing $P(X\\le 6)$ will require us to compute $f(x)$ at $x=0,1,2,…,6.$ However, if we compute the complement $P(X>6)$ instead, then we will only have to compute $f(x)$ at $x=7,$ which will result in a much faster computation.\n\nComputing $P(X>6),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>6) & =P(X\\in \\{7\\}) \\\\  & =f(7) \\\\  & =(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{7}{7})(0.5)^{7}(0.5)^{7-7} \\\\  & =(0.5)^{7} \\\\  & ≈0.0078\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $4$ decimal places.\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 6) & =1-P(X>6) \\\\  & ≈1-0.0078 \\\\  & =0.9922\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $4$ decimal places.",
