      {
        "math_academy_id": "q-98752",
        "knowledge_point_id": "4535b48e-a33f-5f62-95d3-a5c0991c1f6d",
        "knowledge_point": "Classifying Equilibrium Points Using a Graph",
        "problem": "![](images/31/3114d1c94b63a2506a66e701346bc7367b901659b78a2cf7c191648c96a716dc.png)\n\nConsider the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(y)$ where the graph of $f(y)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $y=3$ is a node.\n\nII. $y=-1$ is a sink.\n\nIII. $y=-1$ is a source.",
        "worked_solution": "We can classify the equilibrium solutions of an autonomous ODE ${y}^{′}=f(y)$ by examining its phase line.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *sink* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line both point *toward* the equilibrium solution.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *source* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line both point *away* from the equilibrium solution.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *node* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line point in the same direction.\n\nThe phase line that corresponds to the given graph is as follows:\n\n![](images/f7/f72f89ecad74cc708b5950763002757d9d012d3859c7a5bd5eb19ae60fc54e55.png)\n\nTherefore, we have:\n\n- Statement I is false. From the phase line, we see that $y=3$ is a sink.\n\n- Statement II is false while statement III is true. From the phase line, we see that $y=-1$ is a source.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only\".",
        "answer_fields": [
          {
            "key": "selection",
            "type": "radio",
            "choices_complete": true,
            "choices": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "value": "II only",
                "option": "0",
                "source_option": "a"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "value": "III only",
                "option": "1",
                "source_option": "b"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "value": "I and II only",
                "option": "2",
                "source_option": "c"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "value": "I and III only",
                "option": "3",
                "source_option": "d"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "value": "I only",
                "option": "4",
                "source_option": "e"
              }
            ],
            "correct_value": "III only",
            "value_type": "text",
            "correct_type": "text",
            "evidence": {
              "kind": "worked_solution",
              "value": "III only",
              "source_file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071359/state.json",
              "solution_quote": "Therefore, the correct answer is \"III only\".",
              "matches_worked_solution": true,
